  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="sub">Secret Travel &amp; Tour and VIP Taxi Lanta</p>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: 17 November 2026</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>Zwald Travel Planner Co., Ltd., 292 Moo 2, Sala Dan, Koh Lanta Yai, Krabi 81150, Thailand, company registration no. 0815569000065. The company operates Secret Travel &amp; Tour and sells the VIP Taxi Lanta transfers. Contact: WhatsApp +66 95 868 38 46.</p>

  <h2>2. What this website collects</h2>
  <p>This website has no account and no newsletter. The tour and transfer forms prepare a WhatsApp message on your device and open WhatsApp with it. When you tap “Send on WhatsApp” in a booking form, the website also sends a copy of that request to our booking tool, described in section 5. When you browse, the data handled is technical, such as your IP address in the host's logs (see section 6), plus the audience measurement described in section 3 if you accept it.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">3. Cookies and statistics</h2>
  <p>This website counts visits with Google Analytics 4 and sees how its pages are used with Microsoft Clarity, but only if you accept. A notice asks you when you first arrive. Until you choose, and if you decline, no cookie is set and nothing is sent to Google or Microsoft.</p>
  <p>If you accept:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google Analytics records which pages you view and roughly where the visit comes from: country, type of device, browser and the website that sent you.</li>
    <li>It also records the buttons and links you tap on our pages and where they sit on the page: the WhatsApp buttons, the phone number, the buttons that open a booking form, trip cards and route links.</li>
    <li>When you tap “Send on WhatsApp” in a booking form, we note the trip or route, the option you chose, the number of people and the estimated price shown in the form. We do not record your name, phone number, hotel, dates or the message itself.</li>
    <li>Google Analytics sets two cookies on your device, <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_</code> followed by our measurement ID. They last up to 2 years.</li>
    <li>Advertising is switched off: no advertising cookies, no personalised ads, and your data is not shared for advertising.</li>
    <li>Google processes this data on its own servers, which may be outside your country, under its own privacy policy.</li>
    <li>Microsoft Clarity records how you use our pages: clicks, taps, scrolling and mouse movement. We watch these recordings and the heat maps made from them to see which parts of a page help and which get in the way.</li>
    <li>Everything you type in a form is masked before it leaves your device, so it never appears in a recording: your name, hotel, dates, times and any other text, and the ages of children. The buttons and the options and numbers you choose stay visible.</li>
    <li>Clarity sets its own cookies on your device, <code>_clck</code> and <code>_clsk</code>. Advertising storage stays refused for Clarity too.</li>
    <li>Microsoft processes this data on its own servers, which may be outside your country, under the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your choice is kept on your device, not in a cookie, for 6 months, then we ask again. To change your mind, use “Cookie settings” at the bottom of any page. If you decline after accepting, Clarity stops recording and the Google Analytics and Clarity cookies are removed from your device. The legal basis is your consent.</p>

  <h2>4. Form drafts on your device</h2>
  <p>So that you do not have to type everything again, the tour request form keeps a draft in your browser's storage, on your device only. It is never sent to us. It is ignored after 7 days, and the “Clear form” button deletes it at once.</p>

  <h2>5. What we do with your booking details</h2>
  <p>When you write to us, we receive what you choose to send, such as your name, phone number, dates, pickup place, the number and age of travellers or a flight number. We use these details only to answer you and handle your booking. We share with the partner carrying out the service only the details it needs. We never sell your details or use them for advertising.</p>
  <p id="booking-tool">A copy of each request sent from a booking form is stored in our booking tool, so that the team can handle it. The copy holds the brand (Secret Travel &amp; Tour or VIP Taxi Lanta), the trip or route and the option you chose, the date, the pickup time of a transfer, the number of adults and of children, the pickup place or hotel, the name you typed, the estimated price shown in the form, the address of the page, and the text of the WhatsApp message, which also gives the age of each child. It holds no phone number and no email address. Only the team members who handle bookings can read it. Your IP address is not stored: the tool keeps a scrambled fingerprint of it, only to limit repeated requests. Nothing is sent to an advertiser.</p>

  <h2>6. Services we rely on</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>WhatsApp (Meta) carries our messages, under its own privacy policy.</li>
    <li>Google Analytics measures visits, only if you accept (see section 3), under Google's own privacy policy.</li>
    <li>Microsoft Clarity records how pages are used, only if you accept (see section 3), under the Microsoft Privacy Statement.</li>
    <li>Supabase hosts our booking tool. It stores the copy of your booking request (see section 5) and serves the short notices shown at the top or bottom of some pages.</li>
    <li>Netlify hosts this website and may keep technical logs, such as IP addresses, to deliver it securely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. How long we keep your details</h2>
  <p>We keep your details for as long as we need them to handle your booking, then for as long as Thai accounting and tax rules require.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us at any time to see, correct or delete your details, or object to their use. Write to us on WhatsApp at +66 95 868 38 46. These rights come from Thailand's Personal Data Protection Act B.E. 2562 and, if you live in the European Union, from the GDPR.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the current version. See also our <a href="/terms/">booking terms</a> and our <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>.</p>
  <p class="cookie-link"><button type="button" data-consent-open>Cookie settings</button></p>
